        <div id="faq" class="scroll-mt-24">
          <h2 class="text-3xl font-black text-gray-900 mt-16 mb-6">12. Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
          <div class="space-y-6">
            <div class="bg-gray-50 rounded-2xl p-6 border border-gray-100">
              <h3 class="font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2">Does Scheels sell treadmills?</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm leading-relaxed">
                Yes. On 14 October 2026 scheels.com listed treadmills from NordicTrack, ProForm, Horizon and Landice, and its treadmill category also names Bowflex. Most ship to your home or can be picked up in store; some premium Landice models were marked available in store only. Ranges change, so check the site or call your nearest store.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class="bg-gray-50 rounded-2xl p-6 border border-gray-100">
              <h3 class="font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2">What is the Scheels return policy on treadmills?</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm leading-relaxed">
                Scheels' published policy gives 90 days, with free mail-in returns for online orders and in-store returns with proof of purchase. Items must be in original packaging and condition for a full refund, and shipping fees and surcharges are not refunded. Ask how a freight-delivered treadmill would physically be returned before you buy.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class="bg-gray-50 rounded-2xl p-6 border border-gray-100">
              <h3 class="font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2">Does Scheels price match treadmills?</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm leading-relaxed">
                Yes, at its discretion. The competitor's item must be the exact same brand and model, from an authorised retailer, and in stock on both scheels.com and the competitor's site; competitor shipping is included in the comparison. Used, opened and display items are excluded. Model numbers often differ between retailers, so compare them first.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class="bg-gray-50 rounded-2xl p-6 border border-gray-100">
              <h3 class="font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2">Does Scheels deliver and assemble treadmills?</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm leading-relaxed">
                Scheels ships treadmills as oversized items by freight carrier, with a shipping surcharge shown on the product page, and some ship directly from the manufacturer. We could not confirm a treadmill assembly service on Scheels' pages, so ask the store or the brand, and ask how far the delivery brings the box.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class="bg-gray-50 rounded-2xl p-6 border border-gray-100">
              <h3 class="font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2">Can you try treadmills at Scheels?</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm leading-relaxed">
                In stores with floor models, yes, and that is one of the main reasons to shop there. Floor stock differs between locations, so call the fitness department before visiting. Wear your own shoes, walk and run at your usual speeds, use the incline and fold the machine, and confirm the model number you buy matches what you tried.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class="bg-gray-50 rounded-2xl p-6 border border-gray-100">
              <h3 class="font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2">Where are Scheels stores located?</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm leading-relaxed">
                Scheels listed 34 open stores in 16 states on 14 October 2026, concentrated in the Midwest, the Plains and the Mountain West, from North Dakota and Minnesota to Texas, Utah and Arizona, with four more marked as coming soon. If there is no store near you, scheels.com ships treadmills nationally as freight.
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <!-- Common Mistakes -->
        <div class="mt-16">
          <h2 class="text-3xl font-black text-gray-900 mt-16 mb-6">Common Mistakes When Buying a Treadmill at Scheels</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">None of these is specific to Scheels, but its freight delivery and written policies make each one easy to avoid.</p>
          <div class="space-y-6 my-8">
            <div class="bg-red-50 border border-red-100 rounded-2xl p-6">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-red-900 mt-0 mb-2">Comparing the price without the surcharge</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm m-0">Free shipping over $75 does not cover the oversized-item surcharge. Compare the delivered price with what the same machine costs delivered elsewhere.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="bg-red-50 border border-red-100 rounded-2xl p-6">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-red-900 mt-0 mb-2">Throwing away the box</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm m-0">A full refund needs the original packaging and condition. Keep the box and packing material until you are sure you are keeping the treadmill.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="bg-red-50 border border-red-100 rounded-2xl p-6">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-red-900 mt-0 mb-2">Assuming freight means room delivery</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm m-0">LTL delivery is often to the curb or garage. Ask where delivery ends and who carries the box in before ordering, and plan for the gap.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="bg-red-50 border border-red-100 rounded-2xl p-6">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-red-900 mt-0 mb-2">Asking for a match on a different model number</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm m-0">Price matching needs the identical brand and model. Check the full model number on both listings before you ask, rather than matching a similar-looking machine.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

